// "[Permanent] connives N" [CR#701.50d]: connive N is a variant of connive;
// that permanent's controller draws N cards, discards N cards, then puts a
// +1/+1 counter on the conniving permanent for each nonland card discarded
// this way. Bare "connive" is its own declaration (`connive`), whose body is
// `conniveN(1)`. The permanent "connives" when either process is complete
// [CR#701.50f], so both forms are one deed: this body is enacted as
// `connive`'s (`deed: connive`), and `connive` itself names none. The rules
// instruct the permanent, so, as explore does, a card hands the action to it
// and the body hands the steps on to `controllerOf(actor)`, inside which
// "that permanent" is the conniving one. The discarded cards are read back by
// identity (`discardThenForEachNonland`), so their number is N's; they are
// cards in hand, written `cardIn(hand)` as the owner settled for Burglar
// Rat's discard (2026-10-06). `conniveN` names no deed of its own, so it does
// not read where a deed is wanted; a card names the event `connive`.
// Connive 0 makes no connive event [CR#701.50e], yet `conniveN(0)` is still
// enacted as `connive`: the loader wraps every amount alike. That is the
// rules' to apply, as fight's [CR#701.14b] is, not a guard here: the term is
// what the card says, and the checker is no rules engine
// (`docs/decisions/semantics-v2.md` §7, the checker's charter). Scry 0,
// surveil 0 and endure 0 read the same way.
KeywordAction(
    name: "conniveN",
    params: [Amount],
    spelling: "connive <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "connive",
        frame_set: MeasureComplement,
    ),
    deed: connive,
    body: act(
        controllerOf(actor),
        sequentially([
            draw(Param(0)),
            discardThenForEachNonland(
                counted(exactlyOf(Param(0)), cardIn(hand)),
                putCounters(1, p1p1Counter, that(Permanent)),
            ),
        ]),
    ),
)
